course: dictionary
lesson: 11665
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The man was charged with assault after he hurt a shopkeeper.» Here assault is a serious crime: a violent attack on a person. Hurting someone is against the law.
explain: Now read the next clue. «The runners crawled under nets on the assault course.» Here assault means a training course with obstacles, where people practise strength and speed. Nobody is being hurt. The word course is the clue that changes the meaning.
explain: «The bright lights and loud music were an assault on the senses.» Here assault means a very strong challenge, something that hits your eyes and ears hard. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Assault means a violent attack on a person, and it is a crime.
fact: To assault someone means to attack them violently.
fact: «An assault course» (UK) is an obstacle course used for training.
fact: «An assault on the senses» means very strong sights, sounds or smells.
fact: In battles, an assault is an attack by soldiers to capture a place.
exercise: «The man was charged with assault after he hurt a shopkeeper.» What does assault mean here? | A game played on a sports field | A type of soft music | A kind gift given to a friend | *A violent attack on a person, and a crime
exercise: «The runners crawled under nets on the assault course.» What is an assault course? | *An obstacle course for training | A shop that sells shoes | A road that climbs up a mountain
exercise: «The bright lights and loud music were an assault on the senses.» What does this mean? | A gentle breeze on a warm day | *Very strong sights and sounds that hit you hard | A quiet, peaceful place to rest | Music that makes you fall asleep
test: «The soldiers made an assault on the castle at dawn.» What does assault mean here? | A feast for the king | *An attack by soldiers to capture a place | Sleeping in a tent | A long, slow march home
test: Which word means to attack someone violently? | Greet | *Assault | Describe | Admire
exam: Ella reads that the climbers made «an assault on the mountain». What does assault mean? | A sleepy rest at the bottom | *A strong challenge, a determined attempt to reach the top | A cold drink for the road | A map of the trail
